From 446994432f358b2f52a821b1013bf1a5cfcccbe5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:10:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] hc_read: a second prefill form behind R4D_HC_READ_PF2

The wide prefill form reads h and builds N once per 128-column tile, three
times a call, decodes both E4M3 mixing matrices again in every row tile,
and launches the norm scales on their own. PF2 decodes the matrices once in
a prologue that also computes the norm scales in the same order, runs the
down product one workgroup per 64 rows over all columns with B straight
from WMMA fragment order, and the up product and mix at 256 rows.
R4D_HC_READ_PF2 picks 1 both halves, 2 or 3 one of them, 4 a 128-row down
product. Bit-identical to the wide and the decode tiles' forms; unset, as
before. At M = 2048: 711 -> 611 us a call.
