From c0929b2e79f6b6c97d645dc98b2d1e0ceffa6f2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 09:11:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] hc_read PF2: a persistent up product and mix

Each wave keeps its 16 rows of d as twenty WMMA fragments (K = 320) and the
workgroup walks a run of channel blocks, with mix_up in fragment order so a
block's B is a 40 KB copy into LDS. R4D_HC_READ_PF2 5, 6 and 7 pair it with
the 64-row, the 128-row or the wide down product. Bit-identical. On gfx1201
it is slower than the 256-row tile of value 1.
